{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":73493450,"ns":0,"title":"Active circulator","extract":"In electrical engineering, an active circulator is an active non-reciprocal three-port device that couples a microwave or radio-frequency signal only to an adjacent port in the direction of circulation. Other (external) circuitry connects to the circulator ports via transmission lines.","description":"Active non-reciprocal three-port device","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}